egments: Franchise, Company-owned restaurants, and Rental. The company franchises the restaurants operated by Applebee's franchisees, IHOP franchisees, and Fuzzy's franchisees in the United States. It owns, franchises, and operates restaurant concepts, including Applebee's Neighborhood Grill + Bar within the casual dining category; IHOP in the family dining category of the restaurant industry; and Fuzzy's Taco Shop within the fast-casual dining category. In addition, its Applebee's restaurants offer American fare with drinks and local draft beers; IHOP restaurants provided full table services and food and beverages; Fuzzy's Taco Shop offers mexican food, such as tacos, chips and queso, guacamole, and salsa made-from-scratch daily; and a full bar including margaritas, cocktails, and cold draft beer. The company was formerly known as DineEquity, Inc. and changed its name to Dine Brands Global, Inc. in February 2018. Dine Brands Global, Inc. was founded in 1958 and is based in Pasadena, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John W. Peyton | CEO, Applebee's President & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Dine Brands Global, Inc. Common is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $441M market cap on $879M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 7% cost of capital, a 11-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 46%.","The business throws off $53M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.20\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 20.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 6.5% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (26.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 9% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 47% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"DIN Q3 2026 deep dive: revenue tops expectations, margin pressured by investment and remodels","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nyse/din/news/earnings-call/din-q3-2026-deep-dive-revenue-tops-expectations-margin-pressured-by-investment-and-remodels","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793857310.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Dine Brands Global (NYSE:DIN) Releases Quarterly Earnings Results, Misses Expectations By $0.19 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/dine-brands-global-nysedin-releases-quarterly-earnings-results-misses-expectations-by-0-19-eps.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793851010.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Dine Brands signals track toward low end of full-year guidance while targeting 80 domestic dual brands by year-end (NYSE:DIN)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4665762-dine-brands-signals-track-toward-low-end-of-full-year-guidance-while-targeting-80-domestic","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793829532.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.285,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Dine Brands (DIN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/04/dine-brands-din-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/?source=iedfolrf0000001","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793828427.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.511,"tier":0,"scop